{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"fireless-schematic-gadwall","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# S8 — Cut the production review bot over to Bedrock Claude (dogfood, no fallback)\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nThe `LLM-Review` vote gates every landing on `main`, and today it runs against the direct Anthropic API. Our\nclients will predominantly reach Claude through Bedrock, so the path rebar develops against is not the path\nrebar's users run. Dogfooding closes that gap: if Bedrock throttles, mis-caches, or returns differently shaped\nstructured output, we find out on our own repo before a client does.\n\n## Approach\n\nPoint the review bot at Bedrock-hosted Claude [rebar:2932-8a98-6d70-4550] using the instance-role credentials\nand scoped IAM from S7, with a cross-region inference profile as the throttling mitigation (subject to S3's\ncaching measurement — if caching and inference profiles prove mutually exclusive, this story adopts whichever\nS3 recorded as rebar's documented default and states which). The model stays Claude; only the route changes.\n\n**No cross-provider fallback.** A `FallbackModel` to direct Anthropic would keep landings flowing during a\nBedrock outage, but it would also mask exactly the failures this cutover exists to surface, and it would keep an\nAnthropic key in SSM that the cutover otherwise retires. Instead: the existing tenacity transport retry absorbs\ntransient faults, the existing fail-closed `VOTER_ERROR` path (`src/rebar/review_bot/voter.py:69`) handles hard\nfailure, a CloudWatch alarm fires on `VOTER_ERROR`, and a documented one-line kill switch\n(`REBAR_LLM_MODEL` back to `anthropic:…`) is the human recovery path.\n\n**Alternative rejected: `FallbackModel` to direct Anthropic** — masks the signal the dogfooding is for, and a\npersistently degraded Bedrock could run unnoticed behind a silent fallback.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `infra/compose/` — the bot service's `REBAR_LLM_MODEL` / region environment.\n- `infra/scripts/fetch-secrets.sh` — stop fetching the Anthropic key for this container once the cutover holds.\n- `infra/scripts/observability.sh` — the `VOTER_ERROR` alarm.\n- `infra/runbooks/` — the kill-switch runbook entry.\n\n## Testing\n\nLive end-to-end tier, because this is a cutover of a production gate: the oracle is a real vote on a real change,\nnot a local invocation.\n\n- happy path: a test change pushed to `refs/for/main` receives an `LLM-Review` vote whose sidecar provenance\n  [rebar:343b-4fdc-6722-469b] names `bedrock`, and the review content is substantively comparable to the\n  pre-cutover baseline on the same change.\n- failure path (fault injection at the real seam): temporarily deny the Bedrock IAM statement, push a change, and\n  confirm the bot emits `VOTER_ERROR`, casts no false `+1`, and the CloudWatch alarm fires — then restore and\n  confirm a clean retry produces a normal vote.\n- recovery: the documented kill switch is executed once and shown to restore voting via the Anthropic path.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] a real Gerrit change receives an `LLM-Review` vote produced via Bedrock, with the sidecar provenance\n      showing `provider == \"bedrock\"`, linked in a ticket comment\n- [ ] the same change reviewed pre- and post-cutover yields comparable findings (no new blocking finding that is\n      an artifact of the provider), recorded as a comment\n- [ ] with Bedrock access denied, the bot emits `VOTER_ERROR`, casts no approving vote, and the alarm fires —\n      then a clean retry after restore succeeds\n- [ ] the kill-switch runbook entry exists and has been executed once end-to-end\n- [ ] no Anthropic API key remains in the review-bot container environment after the cutover holds","id":"eb6e-f43a-e86b-443a","parent_id":"061c-ecd1-8967-4a76","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"S8 — cut the production review bot over to Bedrock Claude (dogfood, no fallback)"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785008601319751001,"uuid":"faa084a1-ddcc-478f-a081-5daa5f5d0b1e"}